mmit checks.\n\n**Verdict** (`0cfdc202`, trailer `WI: WI-888`, file `docs/reviews/wi-888/001-ADJUDICATE-3ddee35.md`, `VERDICT: MEANING rows=6`):\n\nEvery row now treats a line as a finding only when its bracket names a declared severity: BLOCKER, MAJOR or MINOR, in any case. Any other bracketed bullet, such as a reviewer's `- [run] lines:` coverage note, is ordinary text. That changes which lines get counted, so code correct under the old text would now fail:\n- **LLR-313 / TC-333:** a `findings=3` review with a `[run]` bullet used to be refused for carrying 4. Now it must be filed, and its rollup shows 3.\n- **LLR-046 / TC-083:** the scorer's finding grammar is now stated, where before the code's catch-all bracket was the de facto rule. That changes every count, tripwire and score built on it.\n- **LLR-069 / TC-069:** the plan-coverage gate's finding numbers no longer shift. In the round-004 example the findings are F1–F3, not F2–F4.\n\n**Why I'd bless them:** the code matches all six. `score_reviews.SEVERITIES` is the one place the severities are declared, and the finding pattern is built from it. `test_prompts.py` checks that the reviewer and critique briefs and PROCESS.md state the same `- [BLOCKER|MAJOR|MINOR] ` grammar, so what the briefs tell a reviewer to write can't drift from what the parser reads. Each new clause has a test.\n\n**Checks run:**\n- The four affected test files: 142 passed.\n- `gen_verdict_rollup.py --check`: fresh across 55 review scopes.\n- `check_trajectory`: clean.\n\n**Observation, not a return:** older review records hold bullets bracketed `[NIT]` (12) and `[FINDING]` (11), and some of their `findings=N` counts included them. Under the new grammar those records count short. The rollups aren't affected, and the RESYNC entry rightly says not to rewrite history. A future tool that re-scores old rounds should treat a mismatch from before WI-888 as a grammar change, not gaming.\n\n**Re-attestation** (`dd2e487c`, act 97): `intake.py snapshot --reattests LLR-046,LLR-069,LLR-313,TC-069,TC-083,TC-333` copied both registries with nothing refused. I edited no registry cells.","ttft_ms":4180,"type":"result","duration_ms":165729,"uuid":"40369e29-7a28-45c8-9597-1c1d1bca9a50","ttft_stream_ms":2526,"time_to_request_ms":323,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":20,"system_prompt":36,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":181,"input_hooks":2,"transcript_persist":1,"tool_pool_refresh":4,"init_message":12,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":17,"message_normalization":17,"client_creation":8,"request_build":16},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":84,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":516,"time_to_request_major_faults":7787,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"changed_files","slowest_producer_ms":167,"cpu_ms":297,"major_faults":3188,"changed_files_reread":6},"first_content_frame_ms":2527,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}]
